{
  "assembly_notes": "Three source records (SOURCES=3) of the same lockable acrylic locker box. The host is a hollow sheet carcass (bottom/top/two sides/back + shelves) closed by compartment_count real side-hinged doors stacked in one column; 1-door-over-a-grid (001) versus N-doors (092616) is a whole-host topology change, so it is expressed as the multiplicity compartment_count rather than as a door_leaf candidate. Five independent structural slots are all directly observed: door_leaf (flat 095210 vs framed 092616), lock (rotary REVOLUTE-Y key + latch lever 001 vs static cam+padlock 092616/095210), hinge (discrete butt stations 001 vs continuous barrel 095210), carcass_front (metal mullions + screws 092616 vs flush edge strips 001/095210) and interior (plain shelves 001 vs shelves + vertical dividers 092616/095210). core_domain = 2^5 = 32, raw_domain = 128. Every combination builds: no compatibility gates. The hinge_line binding is a true cross-slot axis interface \u2014 the hinge slot owns the carcass-side knuckles/pins (provider) and the door_leaf slot owns the door-side knuckle/barrel (consumer); they are coaxial and engage axially by 0.5 mm, so the leaf is genuinely captured, the engagement is rotation invariant, and the overlap depth on the mating axis stays under the 1 mm collision tolerance. No allow_overlap anywhere, and no joint travel is clamped: every door runs 0..1.55 rad, every key +-0.55 rad and every latch lever +-0.65 rad. width_m, depth_m and cell_height_m are honest continuous parameters and do not inflate core/raw.",
